            "notes": "# ROUND 1\n\nReaper has a *grave* problem. Reaper's biggest flaw in Overwatch is his lack of 1v1 potential. Too many characters outrange you, outrun you, or just beat you. But if they can't HEAR you.... they can't win. [Silent As The Grave](item_a2787a6d-3bf5-4d08-b5a5-704aaa053e42) fixes this problem eloquently.\n\nYou COULD start [Strangle Step](item_5af641ec-a231-43ea-ac83-ea15a542e03c) but you're really not gonna get much value out of it. Basically every hero in the game can space, shield, LOS, or sprint away from your 3 seconds of increased [Weapon Lifesteal](stat_weapon_lifesteal). \n\nOur items start out as pretty standard for the meta [Reaper](hero_0449752f-1c58-487b-b9a0-ca727d784457) builds. [Heartbeat Sensor](item_2a4ffaf4-f14b-47d2-a267-0a0e83e87418) gives movespeed and lets us see our victims through their walls. [Running Shoes](item_950eccea-31a0-4a55-8c2a-75bf7920e1aa) is to get into position as soon as possible. Below is a video of proper positioning for round 1. \n\n---\n[Example number 1](https://youtube.com/embed/f-ICVGubVu8)\n---\n\nYou want to be behind the enemies. Make your presence known. Don't hurt them... not yet. Just let them know you could if you wanted to. This will do much more \"damage\" than your left click will at this point.",
